## Clean-room provenance (ADR-021 §3)

This cartridge was **re-created clean-room** from a recorded final-result
baseline — measured geometry, a manifest contract and a prose specification —
**without access to the prior implementation or to its upstream**. The
implementer did not read the removed cartridge, its git history, its archived
satellite repository, or the upstream project's source, models or
documentation.

The prior cartridge under this slug carried a GPL-3.0-or-later origin and was
removed from the commons under ADR-021, which makes CERN-OHL-W-2.0 the commons
licence and a one-way door. Nothing from that implementation is reproduced
here. This is MADFAM's own authoring, in CadQuery, against a published
dimensional standard.

## What is implemented, and what is not

This cartridge is **compatible with the STEMFIE 10 mm block standard**. It
implements the *interface* — the functional dimensions another STEMFIE-
compatible part mates to — and gives everything non-functional a form of our
own. That split is deliberate: ADR-021 §4 notes that where an upstream licence
covers a *design*, reproducing the same shape from a "final result" may still
be derivative. A dimensional standard is not code and not a design; a part
shape is.

### Interface — matched, because interoperability requires it

| Quantity | Value |
| :-- | :-- |
| Block unit (grid pitch) | 10.0 mm |
| Through-hole diameter | 4.2 mm nominal |
| Hole pitch | 10.0 mm = 1 block unit, holes at cell centres |
| Beam cross-section | 10.0 × 10.0 mm per width/height unit |
| Brace plate thickness | 2.5 mm = ¼ block unit per thickness unit |
| Brace arm angle | 90° |
| Fastener shank diameter | 4.0 mm |
| Fastener collar diameter | 5.7 mm |
| Shank-to-hole clearance | 0.2 mm diametral |

### Form — ours, and deliberately not the upstream shape

| Feature | This cartridge |
| :-- | :-- |
| Beam long edges | 0.8 mm **fillet** (the baseline was chamfered) |
| Beam hole mouths | left square |
| Brace outer corners | 2.5 mm radius |
| Brace re-entrant corner | 2.0 mm fillet (the baseline corner was sharp) |
| Brace hole mouths | 0.4 mm × 45° chamfer, both faces |
| Fastener collar | 1.5 mm cylindrical land over a 1.0 mm conical underside taper (the baseline collar was a flat ~2.0 mm ring) |
| Fastener free end(s) | 0.8 mm lead-in taper down to 3.4 mm |

`docs/CLEANROOM-VERIFICATION.md` records the measured proof of both halves:
every interface dimension within ±0.05 mm, every form measurement different.

## Lineage

`project.attribution.lineage` names **the STEMFIE 10 mm block standard
(interoperability only)**. It names no code and no prior implementation,
because none was consulted.

STEMFIE is a third-party project. MADFAM is not affiliated with it and claims
no endorsement by it; the reference is a statement of dimensional
compatibility, in the same sense that a part can be "M4 compatible".
